From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: count AVR lines with the mode's htotal

dpu_encoder_phys_vid_setup_avr() divides the mode's pixel clock by the
INTF's htotal. The INTF timing is halved on a split display and narrowed
by DSC, so the longest frame came out htotal(mode) / htotal(INTF) times
too long: on the dual-DSI DSC TB321FU, 3.7 times, a 92.7 ms frame for a
40 Hz minimum.

Count the lines with the mode's htotal, which goes with its clock;
INTF_AVR_VTOTAL stays in INTF pixels (lines * INTF htotal).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -277,8 +277,15 @@
 	    !intf->ops.avr_trigger)
 		return;
 
-	if (min_hz && htotal)
-		lines = div_u64((u64)clock_khz * 1000, htotal * min_hz);
+	/*
+	 * The clock is the whole mode's: count lines with the mode's htotal.
+	 * The INTF's htotal is smaller on a split or DSC display, and gave a
+	 * frame that many times too long (92 ms instead of 25 ms on the
+	 * dual-DSI TB321FU).
+	 */
+	if (min_hz && phys_enc->cached_mode.htotal)
+		lines = div_u64((u64)clock_khz * 1000,
+				phys_enc->cached_mode.htotal * min_hz);
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(phys_enc->enc_spinlock, lock_flags);
 	intf->ops.enable_avr(intf, false);
